{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>In the morning it flourishes</b> — generation after generation, and it passed, from the root of חליפות שמלות (changing of garments), likewise. If they were slain and it is expounded: 'You send forth Your spirit, they are created' [Psalm 104:30]." "<b>In the morning</b> — and the generation that flourishes and passes is like the weak grass that has no strength in it, that in the evening it withers and dries, and behold He likened the life of man like from morning until evening."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:46.649612549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}